          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %strong topological localization
            is a left exact
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization+of+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} localization of an (∞,1)-category
            – in the sense of passing to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+sub-%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} reflective sub-(∞,1)-category
            – at a collection of morphisms that are
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} monomorphisms
          %p
            A topological localization of an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-presheaves"} (∞,1)-category of (∞,1)-presheaves
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi PSh
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh_{(\infty,1)}(C)
            is precisely a localization at
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cech+cover"} Cech cover
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topology"} Grothendieck topology
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheaves"} of (∞,1)-sheaves
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Sh
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↪
                  %msub
                    %mi PSh
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Sh_{(\infty,1)}(C) \hookrightarrow PSh_{(\infty,1)}(C)
          %p
            and in fact equivalence classes of such topological localizations are in bijection with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topology"} Grothendieck topologies
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %p
            Notice that in general a topological localization is not a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hypercomplete+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} hypercomplete (∞,1)-topos
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hypercover"} hypercover
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            Recall that a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+sub-%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} reflective sub-(∞,1)-category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                  %mover
                    %mo ↪
                    %mover
                      %mo ←
                      %mi L
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D \stackrel{\stackrel{L}{\leftarrow}}{\hookrightarrow} C
            is obtained by localizing at a collection
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            of morphisms of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %p
            The class
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar S
            of all morphisms of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            that the left adjoint
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L : C \to D
            sends to equivalences is the
            %em strongly saturated class
            of morphisms generated by
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/reflective+sub-(infinity%2C1)-category#ExactLocalizations"} recognition principle for exact localizations
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            is exact if and only if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar S
            is stable under the formation of pullbacks.
          %p
            We now define such localizations where the collection
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            consists of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} monomorphisms
            \.
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              Call a morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : X \to Y
              in an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              a
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} monomorphism
              if it is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-truncated+object+of+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} (-1)-truncated object
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/overcategory"} overcategory
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{/Y}
            %p
              Equivalently: if for every object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in C
              the induced morphism in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category"} homotopy category
              of
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} ∞-groupoid
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    C(A,f) : C(A,X) \to C(A,Y)
            %p
              exhibits
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(A,X)
              as a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct summand
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(A,Y)
            %p
              Equivalence classes of monomorphisms into an object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              form a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset"} poset
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Sub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sub(X)
              of
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobject"} subobject
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            This is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} HTT, p. 460
          .num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              The standard example to keep in mind is that of a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cech+nerve"} Cech nerve
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-presheaves"} (∞,1)-category of (∞,1)-presheaves
              the
              %em only
              kind of example.
            %p
              Let
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Diff"} Diff
              be the category of smooth manifolds and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi PSh
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Diff
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh_{(\infty,1)}(Diff)
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-presheaves"} (∞,1)-category of (∞,1)-presheaves
              on
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Diff
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Diff
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} model structure on simplicial presheaves
              on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Diff
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Diff
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Diff
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in Diff
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \hookrightarrow X\}
              be an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+cover"} open cover
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(\{U_i\})
              be the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cech+nerve"} Cech nerve
              of this cover, the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+object"} simplicial object
              of presheaves
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mi ⋯
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mi j
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                      %mo ∩
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi j
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mo →
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                        %mi i
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    C(\{U_i\}) =
                    \\left(
                    \\cdots
                    \\coprod_{i j} U_i \cap U_j  \stackrel{\to}{\to}\coprod_{i} U_i
                    \\right)
                    \\,.
            %p
              which we may regard as a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+presheaf"} simplicial presheaf
              and hence as an object of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi PSh
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn ∞
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Diff
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh_{(\infty,1)}(Diff)
            %p
              Then for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              any other
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi PSh
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
